# EPIC-005 — The Living Universe

Full spec: `docs/EPIC-005.md`

You are creating a **living universe**, not screens. The observatory evolves with time while remaining the same sacred place.

## Environmental channels (layout-neutral)

Moon phase lighting · Seasonal palettes · Particle density · Crystal reflections · Atmospheric intensity · Ritual time (Morning / Afternoon / Evening / Night)

All changes are **opacity and warmth multipliers** — never layout, never readable text impact.

## Ritual time

| Window | Atmosphere |
|--------|------------|
| Morning | Hopeful warmth |
| Afternoon | Neutral clarity |
| Evening | Soft gold-purple |
| Night | Deeper calm |

## Rare events (~14% of days, one max)

Shooting star · Distant glow · Shifting constellation · Golden reflection

Infrequent. Never announced. Never distracting.

## Performance

- Wall-clock state — no perpetual universe animation loop
- One short controller only when a timed event plays
- Lightweight painters, `RepaintBoundary` on event layer

## Before adding environment effects

Pass [Development Charter](./DEVELOPMENT_CHARTER.md) gates. User should feel *"this place never feels exactly the same"* — not *"the background changed."*

## Code

`lib/core/universe/` — integrate via `OraclyUniverseState`, `OraclyUniverseModulation`, `OraclyUniverseLayer`, `OraclyUniverseTicker`.
